1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,661
Dear friends, my name is Odile. You may already know me.

2
00:00:04,661 --> 00:00:08,453
I'm the woman who ran off with the savings circle's money.

3
00:00:09,003 --> 00:00:13,320
Grâce told you her story. Today I'm telling you

4
00:00:13,320 --> 00:00:17,546
mine. Not to excuse myself. To tell the truth.

5
00:00:18,796 --> 00:00:22,369
It was a Tuesday night. The phone rang. My

6
00:00:22,369 --> 00:00:26,199
son Jean-Marc, in Bouaké. A road accident. He

7
00:00:26,199 --> 00:00:30,964
needed surgery, and the hospital wanted the money first.

8
00:00:32,214 --> 00:00:34,815
In my bag was the savings circle

9
00:00:34,815 --> 00:00:38,554
envelope. Grâce's turn. Over a million francs.

10
00:00:39,104 --> 00:00:41,092
I told myself: I'll take it, save my

11
00:00:41,092 --> 00:00:43,688
son, and pay it all back before anyone notices.

12
00:00:44,938 --> 00:00:47,160
I took the night bus. I told no

13
00:00:47,160 --> 00:00:50,098
one. I was too ashamed to call, and every

14
00:00:50,098 --> 00:00:53,036
day I didn't call made the shame heavier.

15
00:00:54,286 --> 00:00:58,110
The surgery worked. My son walks today. But

16
00:00:58,110 --> 00:01:02,646
the money melted away: medicine, the room, therapy.

17
00:01:03,196 --> 00:01:06,477
And meanwhile, eleven families in Abidjan were paying the price of my decision.

18
00:01:07,727 --> 00:01:11,720
He that covereth his sins shall not prosper: but whoso

19
00:01:11,720 --> 00:01:16,378
confesseth and forsaketh them shall have mercy. Proverbs 28:13.

20
00:01:17,978 --> 00:01:22,009
So I worked. Washing clothes for neighbors. Fritters

21
00:01:22,009 --> 00:01:25,653
in the morning. Everything I earned went into a

22
00:01:25,653 --> 00:01:28,521
box with a name written on it: Grâce.

23
00:01:29,771 --> 00:01:32,456
One night I prayed for the first time in

24
00:01:32,456 --> 00:01:35,410
months. I didn't ask God to erase what I had

25
00:01:35,410 --> 00:01:38,162
done. I asked for the courage to go home.

26
00:01:39,412 --> 00:01:42,389
Seven months later I went back to the

27
00:01:42,389 --> 00:01:45,286
market. I had an envelope. It wasn't

28
00:01:45,286 --> 00:01:47,700
all of it. But it was a start.

29
00:01:48,250 --> 00:01:50,675
Grâce looked at me for a long time. Then

30
00:01:50,675 --> 00:01:53,524
she said: I forgive you. I've never heard words

31
00:01:53,524 --> 00:01:55,948
so heavy and so gentle at the same time.

32
00:01:57,198 --> 00:02:01,201
Every month I repay one more family. Four are left.

33
00:02:01,201 --> 00:02:04,811
I keep the notebook myself, and I skip no one.

34
00:02:06,061 --> 00:02:10,044
If you took what wasn't yours, and shame keeps you from

35
00:02:10,044 --> 00:02:15,258
calling, listen to me: shame repays nothing. Neither does silence. Call.

36
00:02:16,508 --> 00:02:19,629
If you're carrying something you can't tell anyone, open

37
00:02:19,629 --> 00:02:22,194
the Community Covenant app. The link is in the

38
00:02:22,194 --> 00:02:25,037
description. Tap Ask for Help and write what you're

39
00:02:25,037 --> 00:02:27,936
going through. A prayer partner answers you, and the

40
00:02:27,936 --> 00:02:30,333
Word is read aloud for the night you're in.

41
00:02:30,883 --> 00:02:34,361
Next week: one year later, the eleven women started

42
00:02:34,361 --> 00:02:37,361
again. Subscribe and turn on the bell so you

43
00:02:37,361 --> 00:02:40,362
don't miss it. Share this story with someone

44
00:02:40,362 --> 00:02:43,362
who needs it. God bless you and your family.
